Subject: Generate scalar array request bodies correctly

Jane 6.3.9 treats every array request body without a generated model as
`array[]` because it reads the PHP type from the array schema itself. For a
valid OpenAPI schema like `type: array` + `items.type: string`, this produces
`@param array[]` and a body guard that only serializes nested arrays.

This patch keeps model arrays unchanged, but for scalar item arrays it:
- derives PHPDoc item type from `items.type`, e.g. `string[]`,
- accepts any PHP array body, including a flat `string[]` or an empty array.

